name:In Processionibus extraordinariis: Oremus. Concede nos; Parce, Domine (orationes);
office-part:Oratio;
mode:;
book:Processionarium O.P. (Cormier), 1913, p. 132 (text: "Deinde, absque Dominus vobiscum, dicat sequentes Orationes praemisso Oremus", with the flexa sign after Orémus, tristítia and castigátus, and colons after gaudére, lætítia, tuo and respíret; neither prayer has its own conclusion: the rubric "Demum subjungat aliquam ex infra positis Orationibus ... eam terminando Per Christum Dominum nostrum" puts the one conclusion after the prayer of the occasion);
commentary:Prayer: Art. III § III, pp. 407-408 ("Modus cantandi Orationes ad Horas, et quotiescumque aliquae aliae Orationes quae non sunt de corpore Officii et Missae cantandae fuerint"), applied after its printed example Concéde nos fámulos tuos (p. 407) and conclusions (p. 408): Orémus h h f, tenor h, at the flexa sign of the text the syllables after the last accent fall to f, at the colon (metrum) the two syllables before the last accent (three if they end a dactyl, Art. III § II 2°, p. 405) on g, the last of them on f, the accent and the rest on h, R. Amen g h (p. 401, VII 2°, p. 408). The inflexions fall where the book marks them on pp. 132-134. F clef on the 3rd line as printed.;
transcriber:the tone printed in the Processionarium O.P. 1913 applied to this text for this site (the book prints this text without notes);
%%
